<title>SWITZERLAND: Foreign &amp; Colonial plans Lebanon stock fund.</title>
<headline>Foreign &amp; Colonial plans Lebanon stock fund.</headline>
<dateline>GENEVA 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>London's Foreign &amp; Colonial Emerging Markets is planning to launch an equities fund for Lebanon's stock market worth up to $50 million, its chief investment officer said.</p>
<p>Arnab Banerji told Reuters during an international investment conference in Geneva on Tuesday that the fund could be launched early in the new year.</p>
<p>&quot;We hope to get around 30-50 million dollars,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>Luxembourg was among the listing options being considered for the new fund, Banerji said but gave no other details.</p>
<p>-- Elif Kaban, Reuters Geneva Newsroom 41-22-733 38 31</p>
